' @guidance:
' Create or update the PlantUML diagram describing how MODULES and PROJECT FILES
' are traversed and processed while performing Act steps (episodes).
' Keep this diagram simple: a short linear flow with minimal partitions,
' one or two decision points, and explanatory notes instead of nested detail.

@startuml
title Ghostwriter - Module & Project File Processing during Act Steps

skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EDF7ED

start

:Scan the project folder;

if (Recursive module processing enabled?) then (yes)
  :Discover and process modules recursively;
  note right
    Each module is scanned like the top-level project,
    including its own files and Act episodes.
    Modules run sequentially or in parallel when enabled.
  end note
else (no)
  note right: Skip module recursion; process only this project's files.
endif

:Collect this project's files;
note right
  Module directories are excluded. Apply configured
  match rules and exclusions; if nothing matches,
  process the project folder itself.
end note

:For each collected file, run the act's episodes;
note right
  Episodes follow the act's selection and order.
  Processing may stop early, skipping remaining files.
end note

:Record the result;

stop

@enduml
